Contributors to zpaq-std
========================

This file lists the people who have contributed code, ideas, or substantial
work to this fork of zpaq-std.

Maintainer
----------
- YadeWira (Yade Bravo) <https://github.com/YadeWira>
  Sole maintainer of the YadeWira/zpaq-std fork.
  Owns the `-ma:algo:N` switch family, the bundled-compressors architecture
  (compressors/), the Makefile, README.md, and WORKFLOW.md.


Upstream lineage (acknowledgements, not contributors to this fork)
------------------------------------------------------------------
- Matt Mahoney — original author of zpaq 7.15 (2009–2016), the deduplicated
  journaling archiver that zpaq-std is built on. <http://mattmahoney.net/zpaq.html>
- The `compressors/` directory contains verbatim source code from:
    * LZ4 by Yann Collet
    * zstd by Yann Collet / Meta
    * fast-lzma2 by Conor McCarthy
    * LZ5 by Przemysław Skibinski / Simon Hahne / Paul Sanja-Luminari
    * Lizard by Przemysław Skibinski
    * bzip2 by Julian Seward
    * bzip3 by Kamila Szewczyk
    * brotli by Google (Jyrki Alakuijala, et al.)
  Each library keeps its original copyright and license. See the individual
  source files in compressors/ for details.

This fork began from the public repository at https://github.com/fcorbelli/zpaq-std
and is a derivative work in the spirit of the MIT license, with substantial
new code by YadeWira (the bundled-compressors architecture, the 9-algorithm
`ma:` switch family, the test infrastructure, and the documentation).
